<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="56932" href="schedule/2014/spring/SCR/115/56932.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2014" href="schedule/2014.xml">2014</calendarYear><term id="120141" href="schedule/2014/spring.xml">Spring 2014</term><subject id="SCR" href="schedule/2014/spring/SCR.xml">Serbo-Croatian</subject><course id="115" href="schedule/2014/spring/SCR/115.xml">South Slavic Cultures</course></parents><sectionNumber>A  </sectionNumber><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>This course explores South Slavic cultures in the historically complex region sometimes referred to as "the Balkans," focusing on the Slavic groups found within the successor states of the former Yugoslavia. We'll examine the ways in which these Slavic groups reject, appropriate, and transform negative stereotypes of their cultures, and position themselves in relationship to "the West."</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2014-01-21Z</startDate><endDate>2014-05-07Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>11:00 AM</start><end>12:20 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>31</roomNumber><buildingName>Psychology Building</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Pintar" firstName="J">Pintar, J</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>